# strapd core package list, restricted to Arch's own core/extra/multilib.
# The ISO builder reads this file when constructing the offline mirror.
#
# AUR packages are in strapd-aur.packages instead, because they need a build
# step and cannot be pacstrapped. Keeping them out is what makes this file
# installable with nothing but a stock pacman.conf.
#
# Why the non-obvious entries are here, so they do not get pruned as unused:
#
#   go-yq             strapd-keybindings-generate reads keybindings/actions.toml
#                     with it.
#   xwayland-satellite  how niri runs X11 apps. Without it every X11 client
#                     silently fails to start.
#   gammastep         warms the screen through zwlr_gamma_control_manager_v1,
#                     which niri, sway and mango all implement, so it needs no
#                     compositor IPC. See bin/strapd-toggle-nightlight.
#   hyprpicker        the name is the only Hyprland thing about it: it is a
#                     wlroots screen-freeze and colour picker, and
#                     strapd-capture-region uses the freeze so a selection
#                     dragged over live content captures what was on screen
#                     when the picker opened. Runs on niri and mango, verified;
#                     on sway too, though it refuses to start without a pointer
#                     device, so the headless rig cannot show it.
#   swaybg            what sway shells out to for `output bg`. It is only an
#                     optdepend, and without it sway logs "failed to execute
#                     'swaybg'" and leaves the desktop black. niri and mango
#                     paint their own backdrop.
#   swaylock          answers strapd-system-lock, which is a key on every
#                     keyboard layout strapd ships. It is the wlroots
#                     ext-session-lock-v1 client, all three compositors
#                     advertise ext_session_lock_manager_v1, and its PAM file
#                     ships with the package and includes `login`, so it needs
#                     no configuration of ours.
#   greetd, greetd-tuigreet  the login screen. tuigreet lists the three session
#                     files strapd installs; swapping it for noctalia-greeter
#                     is one line of etc/greetd/config.toml.
#   noctalia          the shell: bar, panels and OSDs. It draws a bar on each
#                     output, opens an IPC socket, and owns the wallpaper while
#                     running. It does not claim org.freedesktop.Notifications,
#                     which is why mako is also needed.
#   mako              claims org.freedesktop.Notifications, which every
#                     strapd-notification-send call needs a listener for, and
#                     ships a systemd user unit that first-run enables.
#   playerctl         how strapd-media reaches whatever is playing, over MPRIS
#                     directly rather than through a bar.
#   fuzzel            the menu every strapd-menu-* command draws with, reached
#                     through strapd-menu-select alone.
#   niri, sway        two of the three compositors v1 ships. MangoWC is not in
#                     Arch's repos and is in strapd-aur.packages.
#   uwsm              starts a compositor as a systemd user session, and is
#                     compositor-agnostic.
#
# Obsidian is deliberately absent: it is proprietary, so a fresh install boots
# entirely open source and `strapd install obsidian` is one command away. Its
# Arch wrapper flags file lives in default/obsidian/, which only the installer
# reads, rather than config/, which is seeded into every user's home.

